{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nDiscovered from nonblack-brigandish-guillemot: its closing plan review raised this as an advisory finding. After ADR 0125, rebar checks op-certs for validity only unless the verifying environment lists the keys it trusts in `verify.trusted_opcert_keys`. ADR 0125 says that list belongs to each environment's own configuration, not the repository.\n\nNothing enforces that. `verify.trusted_opcert_keys` is an ordinary `[verify]` key (`src/rebar/_config_schema.py`, `VerifyConfig.trusted_opcert_keys`). The CI op-cert gate is the `verify-opcert` step of `.github/workflows/verify-identity.yml`, which runs `rebar verify-opcert` on the checked-out change. `cli()` in `src/rebar/_commands/verify_opcert.py` calls `config.compose_config(root=args.root)` and `trusted_opcert_pairs(args.root)` (`src/rebar/_opcert_verify.py:114`), and both resolve the project layer through `_discover_project_config` (`src/rebar/_config_sources.py:160`), which reads the working-tree `rebar.toml`. So a change under review that adds its own key to `rebar.toml` (or drops `verify.require_environment`) loosens the very gate run that checks it. Reproduced locally: a change listing its own key and closing a ticket under a certificate signed by that key passes `rebar verify-opcert --require-environment <env>` with exit 0.\n\n## Approach (operator decision, 2026-11-20)\n\nThe gate resolves its trust configuration from main's committed `rebar.toml`, never from the `rebar.toml` in the change under review. A change can edit `rebar.toml` freely, but the edit only takes effect for gating after it has itself merged through review.\n\nImplement this in-process in `rebar verify-opcert`, so it holds under any CI provider or none:\n\n- New module `src/rebar/_opcert_gate_config.py` with `gate_config(root) -> (Config, source)`. It composes the same layers as `load_config` (`src/rebar/config.py:483`) — user config, project, env overrides, process `-c` overrides — but the project layer is the project config committed at the reviewed base ref, read with `git show <ref>:<path>`, using the same discovery rule (nearest `rebar.toml`, else `pyproject.toml` with `[tool.rebar]`). The working-tree project config is never read.\n- `base_ref(root)`: `refs/remotes/origin/HEAD` if it resolves, else `refs/remotes/origin/main` (the ref attested gates already treat as reviewed main, `rebar.llm.gate_source.DEFAULT_REF`). A checkout with a remote but neither ref raises `ConfigError` (exit 2) naming the fetch that fixes it: falling back to the working tree there would reopen the hole. A checkout with no remote at all has no reviewed branch and no change under review, so it keeps the working-tree configuration (this keeps local-only projects and the existing remote-less test fixtures working).\n- `cli()` uses `gate_config` for `require_environment`, `opcert_enforce_since` and `trusted_opcert_keys`, and prints the source of the trust configuration to stderr. `trusted_opcert_pairs` is split so the gate can parse a list it already holds (`opcert_pairs(entries)`).\n- `.github/workflows/verify-identity.yml`: the `verify-opcert` step fetches `refs/heads/main` into `refs/remotes/origin/main` (blobless, after the pack measurement) before running the gate.\n- Docs: the `verify-opcert` parser description (regenerated `src/rebar/_cli/help/*.txt` and `docs/cli-reference.md`), `docs/plan-review-gate.md`, and `infra/runbooks/mcp-opcert-enforcement-flip.md` (an enforcement flip takes effect after it merges, not in its own gate run).\n\nNo config key, env var or flag is added: the base ref is fixed at `origin/HEAD`/`origin/main`.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/_opcert_gate_config.py` (new)\n- `src/rebar/_commands/verify_opcert.py`\n- `src/rebar/_opcert_verify.py`\n- `src/rebar/_cli/_parsers/advanced/verify.py`, `src/rebar/_cli/help/overview.txt`, `src/rebar/_cli/help/verify-opcert.txt`, `docs/cli-reference.md`\n- `.github/workflows/verify-identity.yml`\n- `docs/plan-review-gate.md`, `infra/runbooks/mcp-opcert-enforcement-flip.md`\n- `tests/unit/test_opcert_gate_config.py` (new)\n\n## Testing\n\n`tests/unit/test_opcert_gate_config.py`, using a local bare repo as `origin`:\n\n- The attack, end to end: main's committed `rebar.toml` trusts key A; a change branch commits a `rebar.toml` that also lists key B and closes a ticket under a B-signed completion certificate. `rebar verify-opcert --require-environment <env>` exits 1 with `untrusted`, and stderr names the base-branch `rebar.toml` as the trust source. After the change is pushed to `origin/main` and fetched, the same command exits 0. This test fails (exit 0) against the old gate.\n- A dirty working-tree `rebar.toml` and the change's committed one are both ignored; the trust list equals main's.\n- A change cannot drop main's `require_environment`.\n- The environment's `REBAR_VERIFY_TRUSTED_OPCERT_KEYS` still applies (ADR 0125's home for the list).\n- `pyproject.toml` `[tool.rebar]` on main is used when main has no `rebar.toml`.\n- `origin/HEAD` is preferred over `origin/main`.\n- A remote with no fetched base fails closed: `gate_config` raises and `rebar verify-opcert` exits 2 naming `git fetch origin`.\n- A checkout with no remote reads its working tree.\n\nExisting `tests/unit/test_verify_opcert.py` and `tests/unit/test_verify_opcert_ac_coverage.py` (remote-less fixtures) pass unchanged. Full `make verify` before push.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The CI op-cert gate reads `verify.trusted_opcert_keys` from main's committed `rebar.toml`, not the change's: `.github/workflows/verify-identity.yml` fetches `origin/main` before `rebar verify-opcert`, and `gate_config` reads the project layer at that ref (`test_gate_config_ignores_the_working_tree_project_config`).\n- [ ] A change that adds a key to `rebar.toml` does not widen the trust list its own gate run uses: `test_change_adding_its_own_key_does_not_widen_its_gate_run` passes, and fails against the pre-fix `verify_opcert.py`.\n- [ ] No config key, env var or flag is added: `python scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py --check` exits 0 and `git diff origin/main -- src/rebar/_config_schema.py` is empty.\n- [ ] `pytest tests/unit/test_opcert_gate_config.py tests/unit/test_verify_opcert.py tests/unit/test_verify_opcert_ac_coverage.py` passes."}},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1795229406353370001,"uuid":"a51b2d0c-f087-4fd3-9f7d-921ccb2f2d68"}